From 971f0c939d7e0891cb990c4138d102467a3aea5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:51:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hir_typeck: a method found through an associated type's bound
 uses the owning trait for that type

`find_method`'s "UFCS Known, aty bounds" case searches the bounds of
`<T as Owner>::Item` and passed `trait_contains_method` the type as
`<Self as BoundTrait>::Item`: the trait of the bound, not the trait that owns
the item. A supertrait reached through the bound that names `Self` then
carried a projection on a trait without that item. enumset 1.0.12 (jlq 0.1.0):

    pub unsafe trait EnumSetTypePrivate { type Repr: EnumSetTypeRepr; }
    pub trait EnumSetTypeRepr: Copy + Ord + Eq + ..
    impl<T: EnumSetType> PartialOrd for EnumSet<T> { .. self.__priv_repr.partial_cmp(&other.__priv_repr) }

found `PartialOrd<<T as EnumSetTypeRepr>::Repr>` (Rhs = Self, via Ord) and
died with "BUG: src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp:2502: Cannot find associated type
Repr anywhere in trait ::"enumset-1_0_12"::repr::EnumSetTypeRepr". Upstream
code (2025).

It is now `<Self as Owner<I:..>>::Item`, the owner's own parameters as the
impl-level generics that the monomorph state maps to the path's.

Kit aty-bound-supertrait-self-test (enumset's traits, and an owner trait with a
parameter; builds through codegen with a stand-in core).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp b/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp
index 3e41fa9f..80328b73 100644
--- a/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp
+++ b/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp
@@ -5530,8 +5530,12 @@ bool TraitResolution::find_method(const Span& sp,
             ASSERT_BUG(sp, bound.m_trait_ptr, "Pointer to trait " << bound.m_path << " not set in " << e.trait.m_path);
             ::HIR::GenericPath final_trait_path;
 
+            // `Self` of the bound is the associated type: `<Self as Owner<I:..>>::Item`, the trait that owns the item (its
+            // parameters for `monomorph_cb` to fill in), not the bound's trait. That made a supertrait's `Self` argument
+            // `<T as EnumSetTypeRepr>::Repr` (enumset 1.0.12 `type Repr: EnumSetTypeRepr;`, `PartialOrd<Self>` via `Ord`):
+            // "BUG: Cannot find associated type Repr anywhere in trait ::"enumset-1_0_12"::repr::EnumSetTypeRepr"
             auto ty_self = ::HIR::TypeRef::new_path(
-                ::HIR::Path( ::HIR::TypeRef::new_self(), bound.m_path.clone(), e.item ),
+                ::HIR::Path( ::HIR::TypeRef::new_self(), ::HIR::GenericPath(e.trait.m_path, trait.m_params.make_nop_params(0)), e.item ),
                 HIR::TypePathBinding::make_Opaque({})
                 );
             if( const auto* fcn_ptr = this->trait_contains_method(sp, bound.m_path, *bound.m_trait_ptr, ty_self, method_name,  final_trait_path, receiver_fits) )
